Give RLIM_NLIMITS a compile-time value under Cosmopolitan.

Cosmopolitan serves several OSes whose rlimit numbering differs, so it
exposes RLIM_NLIMITS and RLIMIT_* as runtime `extern const` symbols, not
constants. zsh uses RLIM_NLIMITS as a file-scope array dimension
(`struct rlimit current_limits[RLIM_NLIMITS]` in exec.c, mirrored into
exec.epro), which needs a constant expression. Pin it to an upper bound:
the loops that walk the array call getrlimit(i) and tolerate EINVAL for
unused slots, and 16 covers every RLIMIT_* cosmo defines (RLIMIT_AS ..
RLIMIT_SWAP).

--- a/Src/zsh_system.h
+++ b/Src/zsh_system.h
@@ -531,6 +531,10 @@
 
 #ifdef HAVE_SYS_RESOURCE_H
 # include <sys/resource.h>
+# ifdef __COSMOPOLITAN__
+#  undef RLIM_NLIMITS
+#  define RLIM_NLIMITS 16
+# endif
 # if defined(__hpux) && !defined(RLIMIT_CPU)
 /* HPUX does have the BSD rlimits in the kernel.  Officially they are *
  * unsupported but quite a few of them like RLIMIT_CORE seem to work. *
